@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-shared-handoff-requires-verified-foreground-source
The app MUST activate and consume native handoff storage only for its actual verified
eligible foreground source, using the existing shared source namespace. A source or
scene replacement during native reading MUST prevent delivery. Sign-in or confirmed
anonymous state MUST revoke the native handoff audience; checking, network problems,
same-account renewal and scene close MUST preserve durable same-source pending data.
Cross-framework handoff MUST use the bounded canonical payload string, decoded again
in PullyShared before the existing inbox receives its typed destination. Source:
the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native share handoff and account-isolation plan.
